From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] wine.inf: make SysWOW64\drivers, a 32-bit program's System32\drivers

A 32-bit program's C:\windows\system32\drivers is redirected to
SysWOW64\drivers, which Windows has and Wine's prefix did not, so the program
could neither find nor write it. Malwarebytes' setup (a 32-bit installer)
checks that it can write there and refused to install in silent mode (exit
204). The Wow64 fake-DLL section now creates the directory; drivers\etc is
still the shared one.
---
diff --git a/loader/wine.inf.in b/loader/wine.inf.in
index 5bdaf23..ce8b114 100644
--- a/loader/wine.inf.in
+++ b/loader/wine.inf.in
@@ -2411,6 +2411,9 @@ HKLM,%CurrentVersion%\Telephony\Country List\998,"SameAreaRule",,"G"
 [FakeDllsWow64]
 ; create some directories first
 11,mui,
+; SysWOW64\drivers: a 32-bit program's System32\drivers (Malwarebytes' setup refuses to install
+; when it cannot write there)
+11,drivers,
 11,gecko\plugin,npmshtml.dll
 11,Speech\Common,sapi.dll
 11,Speech\Engines\TTS,msttsengine.dll
